{
  "name": "COVID-19's impact on early childhood education and development",
  "parent_id": 203313772661931,
  "group_id": "306d81d9-a33f-49da-acd0-6a19b4d3de64",
  "alternates": [],
  "created_at": "2026-07-30T15:36:56.941Z",
  "deleted_at": null,
  "sort_by_date": null,
  "tag_list": [],
  "updated_at": "2026-07-30T15:36:57.021Z",
  "published_at": "2026-07-30T15:36:57.007Z",
  "id": 203719544625458,
  "uuid": "06994caf-30a3-4bec-b80d-0272a446b01c",
  "is_folder": false,
  "content": {
    "_uid": "157efc03-9010-26d4-cdda-00d72f03dd48",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "b5daaefd-03d5-df32-7819-e3ccd604c864",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Young children reach developmental milestones during these years that include emotional regulation and attachment, language and motor skills. A child's early home environment has long-term effects on their growth and thus any disturbances in the home environment are also likely to impact their development.  ",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "How has COVID-19 affected young children? What can be done to protect them from the effects of COVID-19 and help them to continue to grow in a safe and protected manner? Dr Almina Pardhan, assistant professor at AKU's Institute for Education Development, shared her insights during a webinar.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Click ",
                  "type": "text"
                },
                {
                  "text": "here",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "https://www.facebook.com/akuiedpk/videos/268918697792545/",
                        "uuid": null,
                        "anchor": null,
                        "custom": {},
                        "target": "_blank",
                        "linktype": "url"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": " to watch her talk. Here are some key points from her discussion:",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "Impact of COVID-19 on the development and education of young children",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "list_item",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Young children around the world are most vulnerable with the suspension of important services due to COVID-19. They are also vulnerable because of a potential global recession which risks deprioritising investment for their care, nutrition, health, and their protection and learning.",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "list_item",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "According to UNICEF, experiences from previous shutdowns suggest that children, especially girls, who are out of school for an extended period are much less likely to return to school when schools reopen.",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "list_item",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Closure of schools is also impacting school nutrition programmes driving malnutrition upwards especially in developing countries.",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "list_item",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Early leaners, just like other students, are experiencing interruption and damage to their learning.",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "hard_break"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "What can be done to support young children?",
                  "type": "text",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "bold"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet_list",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "list_item",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Redoubling our commitment to education, including early childhood education, and prioritising our investment in these areas is urgent and critical.",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "list_item",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "It is our collective responsibility to ensure that each child has the best start in life and is protected from the stresses around COVID-19 pandemic for a hopeful future.",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "list_item",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "text": "Increased investments through collective efforts are critical. All sectors, including health, education and other service providers need to work in synchrony to enable the changes needed to support ECED during this pandemic. This is because changes in one domain of early development deeply affect other sectors.",
                          "type": "text"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
